# SciBowl Arena — environment template.
# Copy to .env.local and fill in the placeholders:
#
#   cp .env.local.example .env.local
#
# .env.local is read by Next.js (and by the scripts in scripts/, via @next/env).
# It holds live secrets — keep it out of version control. Restart the server
# after any change; the values are read once at startup.

# ── Clerk — authentication (REQUIRED) ───────────────────────────────────────
# dashboard.clerk.com → your application → API Keys.
# Without both keys the app renders a setup notice and every API route returns
# 503. The publishable key is intentionally public (it ships to the browser);
# the secret key is server-only.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
CLERK_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ── Supabase — rounds, stats, help content (RECOMMENDED) ────────────────────
# supabase.com/dashboard → your project → Project Settings → API.
# Run supabase/schema.sql once in the SQL Editor before starting.
# Leave these unset to fall back to the local JSON store (server/data/db.json) —
# fine for a quick look, but nothing is shared between machines or deploys.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY bypasses row-level security: server-only, never
# prefix it with NEXT_PUBLIC_, and rotate it if it ever leaks.
SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx.supabase.co
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ── Roles (OPTIONAL) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated emails that are always granted the admin role at sign-in.
# Admins are the only ones who can publish public packets. Without this, the
# first user to sign in on a fresh database becomes the admin.
# ADMIN_EMAILS=you@example.com,teammate@example.com

# ── Server (OPTIONAL) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Port for the custom server (Next.js + the /ws realtime channel). Default 3000.
# PORT=3000

# ── Keeping the instance awake (OPTIONAL — free hosts only) ─────────────────
# A free Render service sleeps after ~15 minutes without inbound traffic, and
# its own health checks don't count as traffic. Set this to the app's public
# origin and the server pings itself through it, which does count — so an idle
# spin-down can't land in the middle of a practice session.
#
# Render injects RENDER_EXTERNAL_URL, which is used automatically when this is
# unset, so on Render you usually need neither of these. Leave both unset
# locally and on any paid/always-on host.
#
# Live rooms survive a restart either way (they are mirrored to Supabase and
# restored on boot — see server/sessionStore.js). This only avoids the pause.
# KEEP_WARM_URL=https://your-app.onrender.com
#
# How often to ping, in minutes. Default 10; anything at or over 15 is useless.
# KEEP_WARM_MINUTES=10
#
# 'always' (default) keeps the service up around the clock: 744 h in a 31-day
# month against a 750 h monthly allowance, so exactly ONE service fits and a
# second one will not. 'active' pings only while players are connected — far
# cheaper in instance-hours, still cannot let a spin-down interrupt a game, at
# the cost of a cold start for the first player of each session.
# KEEP_WARM_MODE=always
